        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued November 24 at 1:10PM AKST by NWS Juneau AK",
        "description": "Tidal levels across the panhandle are expected to be running high\nfor the next few days. These high tides combined with passing low\npressures and their associated fronts could create some\npotentially higher than normal water levels. Wind direction,\nmagnitude, and timing with these systems will be monitored closely as\na combination of high tide and winds in an onshore direction\ncould lead to tides exceeding astronomical high tide by a foot or\nmore.",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Observed",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Juneau AK",
        "effective": "2026-11-24T13:10:00-09:00",
        "expires": "2026-11-25T13:15:00-09:00",
        "areas": "City and Borough of Sitka; Western Kupreanof and Kuiu Island; City and Borough of Wrangell; Ketchikan Gateway Borough",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Execute",
        "instruction": "",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      },
      {
        "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7f15d380552b4a026ce6e4f6d32ee31699d642a6.001.1",
        "event": "High Wind Warning",
        "headline": "High Wind Warning issued November 24 at 11:37AM AKST until November 25 at 9:00AM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...South winds 40 to 60 mph with gusts up to 75 mph expected.\n\n* WHERE...Shemya and Attu Islands.\n\n* WHEN...From 1 AM to 9 AM AKST Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...High winds may move loose debris, damage property, and\ncause power outages. Travel will be difficult.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The strongest winds are expected between 5 and\n8 AM AKST Wednesday morning, with winds decreasing, but remaining\nfairly gusty after 9 AM.",
        "severity": "Severe",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
        "sender": "NWS Anchorage AK",
        "effective": "2026-11-24T11:37:00-09:00",
        "expires": "2026-11-25T09:00:00-09:00",
        "areas": "Shemya and Attu Islands",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Prepare",
        "instruction": "People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around\nor damaged by the wind. Prepare for the possibility of widespread\npower outages. Use caution if you must drive.",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      }
    ]
